diseases. Vieta has long been common among Chechens. An exquisite dish was prepared from ground flax seeds — flax halva — by frying flax flour in boiling oil with sugar or honey. This dish was especially appreciated by the Chechens. Chechens cook the dish only with flax seeds. Before the Caucasian War, Chechens, in addition to dishes, also made linen from flax."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-vieta-dish"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vieta_(dish)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Chechen cuisine","cuisine/chechen-cuisine"]]},{"h":"More from Chechen cuisine","links":[["Blini","dish/blini"],["Khingalsh","dish/khingalsh"],["Zhizhig-galnash","dish/zhizhig-galnash"]]}]},"site/nairobikitchen-blogspot-com":{"t":"site","r":"site/nairobikitchen-blogspot-com","n":"Nairobi Kitchen","c":"#55b8ad","crumb":[["Recipe sites","sites"]],"sub":"Recipe site, nairobikitchen.blogspot.com","square":true,"suggested":true,"intro":[["Kenyan recipes blog by Nairobi cook Mulunga."]],"actions":[{"kind":"out","url":"https://nairobikitchen.blogspot.com","label":"Visit nairobikitchen.blogspot.com"}],"sections":[{"h":"Cuisines it covers","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Kenyan cuisine","ref":"cuisine/kenyan-cuisine","color":"#e46a3f","shape":"cuisine","sub":"Nairobi Kitchen","url":"https://nairobikitchen.blogspot.com"}]}]},"cookbook/the-kerala-kitchen":{"t":"book","r":"cookbook/the-kerala-kitchen","n":"The Kerala Kitchen","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Cookbooks","cookbooks"]],"sub":"Cookbook by Lathika George","square":true,"suggested":true,"intro":[["Recipes and food memories from Kerala, published by Hippocrene."]],"actions":[{"kind":"out","url":"https://www.hippocrenebooks.com/store/p497/TheKeralaKitchen.html","label":"Publisher or book page"}],"sections":[{"h":"Cuisines it covers","count":1,"links":[["Kerala cuisine","cuisine/kerala-cuisine"]]}]},"cookbook/zaitoun-recipes-and-stories-from-the-palestinian-kitchen":{"t":"book","r":"cookbook/